validate.prompt:
Check how "{{item.title}}" in {{project}} is really going. It is {{item.status}} and {{item.progress}}% done, planned from {{item.start}} to {{item.due}}, owned by {{item.owner}}.

Notes:
{{item.notes}}

Issue: {{item.issue}}
Pull requests:
{{item.pullRequests}}
Subtasks:
{{item.subtasks}}

Look at the code, the commits and the pull requests to see what is actually done. Propose the progress and status that match, and say what is missing. Today is {{today}}.

reschedule.prompt:
Today is {{today}}. The plan:
{{plan}}

Some tasks are late or start before what they wait for ends. Propose new start and due dates so every task starts after what it waits for, late work is moved to a date it can make, and milestones move only when they have to. Give a reason for each move.

feedback.prompt:
Today is {{today}}. The plan:
{{plan}}

The tasks to look at:
{{items}}

Give feedback on them as a project lead would: missing owners or dates, tasks too big to estimate, dependencies that are missing or wrong, risks nobody tracks. Put feedback about one task on that task and feedback about the whole plan on the plan. Propose changes only where the fix is clear.

breakdown.prompt:
Break "{{item.title}}" in {{project}} into subtasks of a day or two each, planned between {{item.start}} and {{item.due}}.

Notes:
{{item.notes}}

Subtasks it already has:
{{item.subtasks}}

Read the code it touches first. Add each subtask under {{item.id}}, with dates, and make a subtask wait for another where it has to.

status.prompt:
Today is {{today}}. The plan:
{{plan}}

Write a short status update for the people following this plan: whether it is on track, at risk or off track, what moved since the last update, and what needs a decision. Report it as the summary with its health.

work.prompt:
Work on "{{item.title}}" in {{project}}.

{{item.notes}}

Issue: {{item.issue}}
Subtasks:
{{item.subtasks}}

When it is ready, open a pull request that closes the issue if there is one.
